{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792487926,"nonce":"5WE4Qnfdvfx18VWBabVhJoyBYZg=","title":"Release Markdown image residency outside the scroll viewport","message":"Scrolling a visible Markdown document does not release images above or below the viewport. This has two contributing layers. MarkdownView renders every document image eagerly and ties Bitmap disposal to document/tab ownership. Ashui's display-list culling omits records outside the scroll clip but does not dispose Image/Bitmap resources. ImageAtlas retains cached raster entries until overflow reset; reset reuses the texture, and growth is not reversed.\n\nVerified against RayDE's pinned Ashui 418bc4ac36276ca584c1e2c11c599f40dadf1405. Sibling main 4ffe1c2 has identical ImageAtlas source. A standalone Haxe probe creates an Ashui Image in a 400x200 scroll viewport with a 3000-unit spacer; no RayDE extension or VM is loaded. The source raster is shrunk to 800x500. Native bitmap size is queried, the Offscreen display list's image records are counted, and ImageAtlas entries and square texture allocation are measured.\n\nResults:\nvisible: y=0, imageRecords=1, decodedBytes=1600000, disposalCallbacks=0, atlasEntries=1, atlasBytes=1048576\nscrolled-away: y=1000, imageRecords=0, decodedBytes=1600000, disposalCallbacks=0, atlasEntries=1, atlasBytes=1048576\nafter-major-GC: identical to scrolled-away\nowner-disposed: decodedBytes=0, disposalCallbacks=1\n\nThe probe source is bin/image-cull-probe/ImageCullProbe.hx; output is bin/image-cull-probe.log; snapshots are bin/image-cull-probe/image-cull-{visible,scrolled-away,collected}.png. These local diagnostic artifacts are ignored by Git.\n\nRelevant Ashui code: ui/Image.hx retains its bitmap and has no viewport residency policy; types/Bitmap.hx frees decoded pixels only on explicit freePixels/dispose; core/render/Images.hx resolves visible image records; core/render/ImageAtlas.hx caches entries by key, only resets on overflow, and only grows texture capacity. Native blinc_abi b483813 display_list.rs Primitive::push rejects offscreen records without changing bitmap ownership; bitmap.rs BITMAPS holds native pixels until explicit release.\n\nA complete solution needs an explicit opt-in or owned image-resource residency policy, dimensions retained while images are absent, reliable reload when they reenter the viewport, and a bounded/reclaimable GPU atlas. Do not indiscriminately dispose shared caller-owned Bitmaps when one Image is culled. The Markdown extension can avoid eager decode via native metadata/viewport-aware image placeholders; it cannot shrink Ashui's renderer-owned GPU atlas itself. The tab-inactivity cleanup in d7c3d30 is verified but does not solve scrolling residency.","files":null}]}